{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/426818-please-help-me-present-social-merits-in-a-very-nosferatu-way","id":426818,"title":"Please help me present Social Merits in a very Nosferatu way?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-03T12:32:33-08:00","id":426818,"title":"Please help me present Social Merits in a very Nosferatu way?","content":"I'm making a social-focused Nosferatu, and trying to think of ways to present certain social merits in a very Nosferatu way. I mean, Ventrue are just in charge, everyone loves Daeva, and Mekhet blackmail you by existing. What do Nosferatu do? I have some ideas below, I'd love critique and love to hear alternatives.<br /> <br /> <b>Allies:</b> This one is tricky. You can do an &quot;exception to the rule&quot; thing, but I'd rather not. Low ranks can be represented by intimidation factor, easily. People willing to give you Snickers and talk to you about pens. At higher ends that becomes a bit of stretch, unless you go with a &quot;not mummy&quot; thing. (( <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3CkdZeKrO8k\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3CkdZeKrO8k</a> ))<br /> <b>Barfly:</b> Your name is &quot;fucking Brian's coming.&quot; (( <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=o6m42ZQHTfs\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=o6m42ZQHTfs</a> ))<br /> <b>Contacts:</b> They don't want to give you information, but it's the only way to make you go away. No one will actually eject you from the social group (who has the balls?).<br /> <b>Retainer/Staff:</b> Just pointing out that a dot in Staff [Persuasion] lets you sidestep the nosferatu angle for Allies and Contacts. A similar result can be achieved with Retainer. You have very intimidated people that work for you and get information / etc. for you. As an aside, what are some good things for Staff [Persuasion] to represent?<br /> <b>Sympathetic:</b> You think you have the upperhand. Maybe you really do. It's not going to last long. It's the part of the horror movie just before the final twist of the knife, where everyone thinks everything is okay.<br /> <b>Striking Looks:</b> Getting a Striking Looks that applies to Intimidate rolls is easy. How to do you get one that applies to a reasonably number of Persuasion, Socialize, or Subterfuge [lying]? I'm particularly looking for subterfuge, for this character.<br /> <b>True Friend / Touchstones:</b> Just noting these here because I believe, by and large, if you're going to have exceptions to the rule, this is the place to do them.<br /> <br /> So yeah, what are some examples of nossy characters with lots of social merits? How do they all fit together into a cohesive, vaguely horror-movie-like whole? Either at your actual table, NPCs, or theory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 03-03-2015, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T13:49:45-08:00","id":426963,"title":"","content":"For a nossie take on Striking Looks (Subterfuge), how about the character looking remarkably unsubtle? Nobody expects a guy who looks like Sloth from The Goonies to lie to them because they assume, based on his appearance, that he's not socially skilled enough to pull it off. They believe that on the off chance you actually try to lie to them, it will be painfully obvious; so they don't even bother looking for subtle tells or cues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T13:54:02-08:00","id":426965,"title":"","content":"Allies and Contacts: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>You are the Mystery Man. They only know you by a voice over the phone or internet or maybe mysterious letters. You have helped them at times and they know they have to return the favour to keep on your good side.</li> <li>You have personally helped someone really high up in the hierarchy. Maybe she owes you her life? The organisation overlooks your unsettling presence</li> </ol><br /> Staff [Persuasion]: Lobbyists, for example.<br /> <br /> Retainer: Could always be a ghoul or thrall.<br /> <br /> Striking Looks: Maybe there is something about that character that makes him both horrifying, but strangely compelling, like an adroit devil haggling for your soul. You know you really should not get involved with this guy and once that nagging voice in your head wins out, you'll be gone (Curse-caused Dramatic Failure), but until then you are drawn to this infernal guy in spite of yourself. Alternatively, consider those Nosferatu that looks presentable, perhaps even beautiful, but their aura is simply unsettling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T16:48:25-08:00","id":427107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/426818-please-help-me-present-social-merits-in-a-very-nosferatu-way?p=426965#post426965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Allies and Contacts:<br /> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>You are the Mystery Man. They only know you by a voice over the phone or internet or maybe mysterious letters. You have helped them at times and they know they have to return the favour to keep on your good side.</li> </ol><br /></div> </div> </div> </div><i>Angel of music, guide and guardian, grant to me your glory! Angel of music,</i><i> hide no longer, come to me strange angel!</i><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}